## Production code

  + internal/ai/features/registry.go
      Added `cross-rule-conflict-detection` feature entry between
      inbox-auto-categorization and `__redaction_bypass__`.
      DefaultOn=false, DependsOnFeatures=nil, AllowedTools=
      ["query_alert_rules","detect_rule_conflicts"], all RouteSet
      fields populated explicitly (JobNames=[]string{},
      PushKinds=[]string{} — never nil).

  + internal/ai/strategies/cross-rule-conflict-detection/strategy.go
      Strategy port impl. SystemPrompt mandates the typed
      query→detect→narrate sequence + closed-taxonomy + structural-
      overlap-not-prediction qualifier. AllowedTools defensive copy.
      RedactionPolicy = redact.PolicyAlertBuilder (REUSED — alert
      rules are DTOs with no PII; deny-all is the correct policy).
      EvalGoldens=nil; loaded out-of-band by the eval harness from
      goldens.yaml.

  + internal/ai/strategies/cross-rule-conflict-detection/goldens.yaml
      3 deterministic goldens:
        typical_overlapping_thresholds — happy path; query → detect →
            narrate; LLM must surface the closed taxonomy + honest
            structural-overlap-not-prediction qualifier.
        no_conflicts_clean_set         — empty conflicts list; LLM
            must narrate "no conflicts" without inventing one.
        refusal_other_user             — wrong scope; LLM must NOT
            call any tool, must refuse + explain.

  + internal/ai/strategies/cross-rule-conflict-detection/canned/*.yaml
      Three canned mock-provider replies (FIFO sequence:
      query tool_call → detect tool_call → final stop frame).

  + internal/ai/tools/cross_rule_conflict.go
      Two propose-only F4 tools (query_alert_rules,
      detect_rule_conflicts) sharing one narrow port
      (CrossRuleConflictSource). Pure-functional `DetectRuleConflicts`
      detector with closed taxonomy + numericInterval projection
      (sentinel-bounded segments + epsilon round-trip). Defensive
      copies on tool args to keep the LLM's mutation surface zero.

  + internal/api/ai_cross_rule_conflict_handler.go
      AICrossRuleConflictHandler wires the strategy through the
      F1 dispatcher, exposing it via the standard /api/v1/ai/...
